WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.172 --> 00:00:10.940
Can you tell us what it was like

00:00:11.073 --> 00:00:12.508
having that many folks there,

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.177
and sleepy folks and people that

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.078
needed just comfort and how you

00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:17.914
dealt with it?

00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:20.516
&gt;&gt; It was absolutely crazy

00:00:20.516 --> 00:00:24.520
having so many people from so

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.721
many different nationalities in

00:00:25.855 --> 00:00:26.522
one room.

00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:33.262
I think a lot of people think it

00:00:33.396 --> 00:00:35.932
was our local patrons and guests

00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:36.933
stuck here.

00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:40.670
There was not more than my

00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:43.639
left-hand man and right-hand man

00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:45.508
here that were local, and the

00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:48.544
rest were out of Canada, out of

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:49.779
state and from around the

00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:50.412
country.

00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:52.014
They came together and they were

00:00:52.148 --> 00:00:54.817
washing dishes and bussing

00:00:54.951 --> 00:00:55.284
tables.

00:00:55.284 --> 00:00:56.819
It was a sight like no other.

00:00:56.953 --> 00:01:05.394
As you said, we are -- it's old,

00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:08.831
and we have a dining room that

00:01:08.965 --> 00:01:10.566
can accommodate approximately

00:01:10.566 --> 00:01:13.102
100 people, and we brought in

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:15.571
115 people.

00:01:15.705 --> 00:01:18.040
&gt;&gt; Truly, you likely saved

00:01:18.174 --> 00:01:18.641
peoples' lives.

00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:21.978
We are seeing the result of the

00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:23.312
cold temperatures and people

00:01:23.446 --> 00:01:24.580
being stuck in cars.

00:01:24.647 --> 00:01:25.882
Your Facebook page is covered

00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:29.218
with people who are so so

00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:30.586
thankful because of what you

00:01:30.586 --> 00:01:33.923
did, like this one from Lynn

00:01:34.056 --> 00:01:34.556
becca.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.225
She writes the true meaning of

00:01:36.592 --> 00:01:38.928
Christmas.
People from all over, different

00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:40.162
backgrounds and different

00:01:40.596 --> 00:01:41.998
beliefs but united as one.

00:01:42.131 --> 00:01:43.866
Nothing but smiles, no worries

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.903
in that very moment.

00:01:47.036 --> 00:01:49.605
Rested, full bellies, warm and

00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:50.940
sheltered thanks to the great

00:01:51.073 --> 00:01:52.975
community members of Alabama

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:55.845
hotel.
This is seriously the best

00:01:55.978 --> 00:01:59.148
blizzard of 2022 story ever.

00:01:59.282 --> 00:02:01.317
How did you spend the two days

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:01.817
yourself?

00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:02.818
Please, tell me the names of the

00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:05.454
folks that were there to help

00:02:05.588 --> 00:02:06.622
everybody feel comfortable?

00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:12.061
&gt;&gt; So I spent the two days

00:02:12.194 --> 00:02:16.732
awake, very awake, and tired at

00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:19.035
times.
Craig Alexander from the Alabama

00:02:19.168 --> 00:02:20.069
holly farms across the street

00:02:20.202 --> 00:02:24.173
was here with me.

00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:25.841
He was just trudging through the

00:02:25.975 --> 00:02:29.045
snow back and forth to the meat

00:02:29.178 --> 00:02:31.013
market, bringing us more food

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:32.782
when it was necessary.

00:02:33.516 --> 00:02:37.219
I had Brian from B &amp; K

00:02:37.353 --> 00:02:38.120
construction, and he was one of

00:02:38.254 --> 00:02:40.323
the locals that was here all the

00:02:40.656 --> 00:02:42.091
time and his daughter was

00:02:42.224 --> 00:02:44.160
involved in an accident up the

00:02:44.293 --> 00:02:45.828
street that brought him in, and

00:02:45.962 --> 00:02:47.563
little did he know he would be

00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:51.067
working side by side with me for

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.668
48 hours.

00:02:52.668 --> 00:02:54.937
&gt;&gt; That's really beautiful to

00:02:55.071 --> 00:02:55.571
here.

00:02:55.571 --> 00:02:59.108
&gt;&gt; The whole community, the

00:02:59.241 --> 00:03:02.078
women just a few doors down,

00:03:02.211 --> 00:03:04.680
came through the snow pulling

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.249
two sleighs of blankets, pillows

00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:09.151
and air mattresses.

00:03:09.285 --> 00:03:10.686
The community members that

00:03:10.786 --> 00:03:12.355
dropped off Christmas presents

00:03:12.688 --> 00:03:13.489
so these children had something

00:03:13.623 --> 00:03:17.093
to open up on Christmas morning.

00:03:17.226 --> 00:03:19.962
Just crazy, crazy, absolutely

00:03:20.096 --> 00:03:23.466
crazy how everybody came

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:24.000
together.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.104
This place ran like a smooth

00:03:28.237 --> 00:03:30.339
oiled machine.

00:03:30.706 --> 00:03:32.274
We served a lot of food, and not

00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:34.176
only did we serve a lot of food,

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.246
we served about 60 pounds of

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.716
prime rib, and these folks had a

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.552
prime rib dinner on Christmas

00:03:43.686 --> 00:03:46.756
eve.
That's thanks to Bonnie, and I

00:03:46.889 --> 00:03:49.125
said I fed these guys so much

00:03:49.258 --> 00:03:52.728
food, and she said break out the

00:03:52.728 --> 00:03:53.562
prime rib, so we did.

00:03:53.696 --> 00:03:56.732
&gt;&gt; That is so beautiful.

00:03:56.732 --> 00:03:57.633
Just lovely to hear people

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.069
coming together like that in a

00:04:00.202 --> 00:04:02.171
place where we're kind of

00:04:02.304 --> 00:04:03.539
fractured on some levels.

00:04:04.206 --> 00:04:06.742
I wanted to quickly ask you

00:04:06.742 --> 00:04:09.879
about a father named Nico, and

00:04:10.012 --> 00:04:12.348
he was stunned and said you

00:04:12.748 --> 00:04:14.750
saved the lives of he and his

00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:15.151
family.

00:04:15.151 --> 00:04:16.752
Tell us stories about some of

00:04:16.752 --> 00:04:17.753
the people and what they were

00:04:17.887 --> 00:04:19.622
facing and why they ended up

00:04:19.755 --> 00:04:22.258
there at your restaurant?

00:04:22.391 --> 00:04:24.160
&gt;&gt; So it's my understanding that

00:04:24.293 --> 00:04:26.429
most of these people ended up at

00:04:26.762 --> 00:04:29.665
the restaurant because they were

00:04:29.799 --> 00:04:32.768
on the thruway and the thruway

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:36.238
was closed and they got off and

00:04:36.372 --> 00:04:38.774
most of them were driving

00:04:38.808 --> 00:04:40.776
towards Canada, and some folks

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.346
just ended out front because

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.315
there was a sign that said

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:51.220
hotel, and some used Google and

00:04:51.353 --> 00:04:54.123
it said we were a hotel offering

00:04:54.256 --> 00:04:54.756
rooms.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.058
They just started pouring in.

00:04:56.192 --> 00:04:57.993
I don't know what else to say.

00:04:58.127 --> 00:05:00.196
They just started pouring in and

00:05:00.329 --> 00:05:01.564
it started with one or two

00:05:01.697 --> 00:05:03.365
people, and then a few minutes

00:05:03.499 --> 00:05:05.768
later it was 10 people, 15

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:06.235
people.

00:05:06.235 --> 00:05:08.003
And a lot of these people were

00:05:08.137 --> 00:05:11.841
rescued off the side of the road

00:05:11.974 --> 00:05:16.812
by the state police, and the

00:05:16.812 --> 00:05:19.815
transportation department, and

00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:23.619
helping to get people here and I

00:05:23.753 --> 00:05:29.425
do -- I do believe we saved a life or two.

